{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_12b749dc1f0360ef014f0c64bbc9a34af1029f8baef28c4f52cab1799af67eff","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_33c0ba8e0a39ada27282b120f1a61fc4c1b04cdc2b165b62485c00f9fbe9ba96","slc_fd24ea0304c3bc6d7966e7a676d14f6dd35882e3c4951e1cf5059c1d5a9f5d71"],"source_ids":["src_a8c4bbb666585a6a85316b670ce64910"],"text":"The methodology mandates a test-first gate for AI-generated code: write tests, confirm they fail and commit that state, then implement without modifying test files.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1c90b86d4e8b96db524ccf6dcd9f644b80fcb71a713068a8aa99dca13fd6d17b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0245fc10e91342b3fc972c22b3d9d5c79647f7a3f49ccd24c5fdcff83fbe57fb","slc_43d842e7fda9bb8a617cee7299c8cdafb4ea329aaad7cd2ba34a6ba08b294bd9"],"source_ids":["src_422bf43bb6c7517498436983e31c26c6","src_842d991c73375108b27a474a2492c958"],"text":"The toolkit prescribes a traceable artifact chain — PRD (what), SPEC (how), ADR (why), TASK (steps) — flowing through code, review, deploy, and closed by a sprint retrospective.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_27451c3268805d2a8496acaa1f7f12edf909de6bba7c96be5d90dfd8a709318f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_41daaa0801464db0a8ec530b7778c1f35a1fe2094ad0268b89c05e749c87d461","slc_5b9df057c9f7471e5d9837794e5be9c9a2036490f9e2c5b0d16464e69ebfb7e8","slc_97d30d555a44bf5e945b830ab64c538cd4104c272ca4efd235f9f5021c41ba7b","slc_f837c2d27f86c6bdb30cd6ef846e45ee75ccf0409a90283b3a5e21d4582d71ad"],"source_ids":["src_842d991c73375108b27a474a2492c958"],"text":"Beyond standard ADRs, the toolkit defines three AI-native ADR categories — model selection, prompt strategy, and agent orchestration — each with its own template.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3c7ce68dbbf6eee3d825392e647d9a80732755843ada1872d762ea421e26cc1d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_76ae4502a3a1604aa241083023547dff429f7e28f91db323aaa02fab6c9c25a2"],"source_ids":["src_842d991c73375108b27a474a2492c958"],"text":"Traceability links are asymmetric: children reference parents (e.g., SPECs reference parent PRD-NNN; TASKs reference spec and ADRs), while PRDs reference nothing upstream.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4949b5e8e914295888f8c48e7d8702fc6ce3eca18815cc1c8d3e26dda8ada960","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_268688f98c04bcceb36649db68468f40a4a2a4592ee48a6c0893a71f0f719194"],"source_ids":["src_535bf78b4ecb55d1b1cb469439d35d2f"],"text":"Skills in .claude/skills/ are exposed as available slash-commands in Claude Code, and path-scoped rules in .claude/rules/ load when relevant files are opened.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_593672f44c90e85d98355683a3e2fc7479392707d952363053aa7e9dcbbf2c30","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_817db3f6ad590af508d4374ebd0e726b7ed7d0d2f329146366dd965ca1af50da"],"source_ids":["src_535bf78b4ecb55d1b1cb469439d35d2f"],"text":"Prerequisites listed are Claude Code (installed via npm), Node.js 18+, configured Git, a GitHub account, and optionally RuFlo for multi-agent orchestration.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5f36c5ea8b6ce0a874be89d00de2a3c9c45d6479e32ba7b4c75b8ea395571645","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4482fe661f9f9a8e6e1e61e29b52c1ea9a68720f01eaefc262a7487d55f0e962","slc_ae8cd6387191558fc21343ab0f9ccf12ea9ed3a5083daae1e0b9991a6d5ced05"],"source_ids":["src_842d991c73375108b27a474a2492c958"],"text":"Every artifact carries a traceability ID in YAML frontmatter with defined formats such as PRD-NNN, SPEC-NNN, ADR-NNN, TASK-NNN, S-NN, and PV-NNN.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7fc09b5b0759d72c0499d8cf22b7d2352a6042e18241b3089ba761325f1831d3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2584ad299a66befc046da946208fe4636039c35a66838dda604fafe7fe5c2b99"],"source_ids":["src_842d991c73375108b27a474a2492c958"],"text":"The repository ships copy-and-fill templates including PRD, SPEC, TASK, sprint plan, and four ADR variants: core MADR-style, model-selection, prompt-strategy, and agent-orchestration.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_963c787ab7734db7a8ac55e168c1b2a9805c3d78d97907350bd2021e61dae5a5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2cade6207b343d5b5aacc3f704923ec654cbe2e4c6c54b0a9047255880f79d89"],"source_ids":["src_535bf78b4ecb55d1b1cb469439d35d2f"],"text":"The init.sh setup script updates CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md, creates a project ADR registry, initializes the first sprint folder, adds .gitignore entries, and installs pre-commit hooks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a62a0b97bad6c36191699dc2cdf0c0e2576a5162cbc4d85f869a3020fae4cff5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_29d4bcb54a10fc1fc4f0d42b793e482d74ac07f0d3b63239ec2f6d443073a4e0","slc_ffc8ae4670038874d3cc22c8445ca60806f887264dd0ae6a0af539d0225c3ac7"],"source_ids":["src_535bf78b4ecb55d1b1cb469439d35d2f","src_842d991c73375108b27a474a2492c958"],"text":"The methodology assigns RuVector the role of maintaining persistent memory across sessions so agent context does not start cold; RuFlo optionally orchestrates agents across the artifact chain.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c4b1ff73576888c48feeb92f86ad5c0a074f1abb8d16c1b66019a397cc770dcf","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_249b941594a7afcefd4879fffa8c4febf4a0e0fd2c124cb2591d3ab863b9a638","slc_a9f329659df859b6b56e9f447fb4638e11e750eb5eb62e3bccea54e778d4c7f9"],"source_ids":["src_842d991c73375108b27a474a2492c958"],"text":"The toolkit is released under the MIT License, with copyright attributed to BarryHurd.com.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c5698cc0922bb2b43e84506d7ff25c6d2666d1f57189c5abd5f82b9172ca83c7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5b2c15891b1b94eb70afbf9f1adbd3abdf67ada8f14d86e3693842e903213833","slc_d5d8664d657a97813634dfb389cbd0cd064e2efc930b7a43672596e62c27f1b3"],"source_ids":["src_a8c4bbb666585a6a85316b670ce64910"],"text":"For AI-native features, the methodology prescribes running a promptfoo eval suite before merging, with the pass threshold defined in the feature's SPEC acceptance criteria; unmet thresholds mean the task is not done.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dfe5c310551a8491fba786290eca9de173a77b7e8ec36553d5581f721ae32a9b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"polymathwizard/bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit@161f8e5311bd snapshot dffb30bc95fe376f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5ddca09a8f59c821d303186872965cc75b0f80e08eb9ea4361efd8a594451ecd","slc_c68f896de4949195e2b5fa15f708efa5c5cb601126bffaea15a0684caf9620ac"],"source_ids":["src_a8c4bbb666585a6a85316b670ce64910"],"text":"A sprint is defined as a two-week cycle with four phases: specification (days 1-2), planning (days 3-5), implementation (week 2 days 1-3), and integration/evaluation/deploy/retro (days 4-5).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
